ing Education\nL298:   * cite131†Disability Access CE Notice of 2nd Modified Text L299:   * cite132†Disability Access CE Second 2nd Modified Text L300:   * cite133†Notice of Modified Text L301:   * cite134†15–Day Modified Text L302:   * cite135†Notice of Proposed Regulatory Action L303:   * cite136†Proposed Regulatory Language L304:   * cite137†Initial Statement of Reasons L305:   * cite138†Final Statement of Reasons L306:   * cite139†Order of Adoption L307:   * cite140†Notice of Approved Regulatory Action L308: Filed with the Office of the Secretary of State: January 17, 2023\nL309: Regulatory Action Effective: January 17, 2023\nL310: ## CCR Section 160—(section 100)\nL311: \nL312: Rules of Professional Conduct\nL313: \nL314:   * cite141†Section 100 Justification L315:   * cite142†Notice of Approval with Deleted Text L316: ## CCR Section 112 (repeal)—(section 100)\nL317: \nL318: Processing Times\nL319: \nL320:   * cite143†Section 100 Justification L321:   * cite144†Notice of Approval with Deleted Text L322: \nL323: Back to top\nL324: \nL325:   * cite145†Back to Top L326:   * cite146†Conditions of Use†www.ca.gov L327:   * cite147†Privacy Policy†www.dca.ca.gov L328:   * cite148†Accessibility L329:   * cite149†Accessibility Certification L330:   * cite2†Contact Us L331: \nL332: Copyright © State of California\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn1216view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1185view0\",\"id\":29}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?data=05%7C02%7COALPostedRegsLink%40oal.ca.gov%7C43ab534f38b94490c7ec08def18503d5%7Cea45f7b107d749a8b8f537136ec9382d%7C0%7C1%7C639213750812764761%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&reserved=0&sdata=B8FZuvhpd6VC2d1JYTSPrlV8thmS%2BcGx82j2DdLB%2FtU%3D&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.brea.ca.gov%2Fpdf%2Faqbednoticeofapproval07152026.pdf: (400) Bad Request\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFinal Text of Regulations - 649.26, 649.29.1, 649.29.2 (https://victims.ca.gov/uploads/Final-Text-of-Regulations-649.26-649.29.1-649.29.2.pdf)\nciteturn1216view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 9; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1188view2\",\"id\":23}); Total lines: 236\nL0@P0: CALIFORNIA VICTIM COMPENSATION BOARD\nL1@P0: TEXT OF REGULATIONS\nL2@P0: PROPOSED AMENDMENTS TO CALIFORNIA CODE OF REGULATIONS\nL3@P0: TITLE 2. ADMINISTRATION\nL4@P0: DIVISION 2. FINANCIAL OPERATIONS\nL5@P0: CHAPTER 1. CALIFORNIA VICTIM COMPENSATION BOARD\nL6@P0: ARTICLE 5.6. INDEMNIFICATION OF VICTIMS OF CRIME\nL7@P0: SECTIONS 649.26, 649.29.1, and 649.29.2\nL8@P0: Proposed Text: Page No.:\nL9@P0: Section 649.26 Direct Payments to Providers .................................................................... 1\nL10@P0: Section 649.29.1 Mental Health Benefits............................................................................... 3\nL11@P0: Section 649.29.2 Dire or Exceptional Circumstances and Specialized Mental Health\nL12@P0-1: services ...................................................................................................................................... 8 1\nL13@P1: § 649.26 Direct Payments to Providers\nL14@P1: (a)If the VCP When the Board authorizes direct payment to a healthcare provider\nL15@P1: of VCP services or mental health provider of CalVCB services, the VCP Board\nL16@P1: may require the provider to submit bills using CMS 1450, CMS 1500 or American\nL17@P1: Dental Association bill forms for verification of services provided. Applicants\nL18@P1: Claimants are not required to use the above-noted forms to request\nL19@P1: reimbursement of eligible pecuniary losses that they paid.\nL20@P1: (1) Mental health providers must submit the information as detailed in\nL21@P1: §649.29.1 (b)(1)-(9) either in advance of or along with their first bill or CMS\nL22@P1: 1500. Sessions may be reimbursed once the required information has been\nL23@P1: provided to and approved by the Board.\nL24@P1: (2) All bills must be submitted to any and all available insurance, benefit\nL25@P1: programs, or other reimbursement sources prior to being submitted to the\nL26@P1: Board as CalVCB is the payor of last resort. If an expense is not otherwise\nL27@P1: covered, or is only partially covered, providers must submit a copy of the\nL28@P1: Explanation of Benefits (EOB) or other verification from the insurer, benefit\nL29@P1: program, or other reimbursement source, documenting the denial or\nL30@P1: partial payment along with the CMS 1500. No payment will be made until\nL31@P1: all other potential reimbursement sources are exhausted and the\nL32@P1: necessary information regarding efforts to seek reimbursement from other\nL33@P1: sources is received.\nL34@P1: (b)The VCP Board shall inform the victim or derivative victim claimant of his or her\nL35@P1: their right to object to direct payments by VCP CalVCB to providers of services in\nL36@P1: accordance with Government Code section 13957.7(c)(1). In the event that the\nL37@P1: victim or derivative victim claimant asserts such right the VCP Board may\nL38@P1: reimburse pecuniary loss to the victim or derivative victim claimant only in\nL39@P1: amounts equal to sums actually paid out by the victim or derivative victim\nL40@P1: claimant to the service provider and only upon submission by the victim or\nL41@P1: derivative victim claimant of evidence of such payments, subject to the rates\nL42@P1: and limitations set by the Board in accordance with applicable law. Following\nL43@P1: such an objection, direct payment shall be made to the provider only upon a\nL44@P1: demonstration of good cause as determined by the board.\nL45@P1: (c)For consideration of payment for mental health counseling over the claimant's\nL46@P1: authorized session limit, mental health providers must submit the VCP Treatment\nL47@P1: Plan and the VCP Additional Treatment Plan for review and approval within 90\nL48@P1: days of the date VCP receives the bill for sessions that exhaust the claimant's\nL49@P1: authorized session limit providers must submit the information outlined in\nL50@P1: §649.29.1 (e)(1)-(13) to the Board for approval before additional sessions may be\nL51@P1-2: considered for payment. If the VCP Treatment Plan and VCP Additional 2\nL52@P2: Treatment Plan are not submitted within the 90-day timeframe, bills for all dates\nL53@P2: of service that exceed the authorized session limit will be returned and will not\nL54@P2: be considered for payment. However, bills for dates of service provided after\nL55@P2: the VCP Treatment Plan and VCP Additional Treatment Plan are received may\nL56@P2: be considered if the VCP Additional Treatment Plan is approved and the\nL57@P2: authorized session limit is increased.\nL58@P2: (1) Providers must submit the information to the Board for review and\nL59@P2: approval within 90 days of the date the Board receives the bill for sessions\nL60@P2: that exhaust the claimant’s authorized session limit. If the required\nL61@P2: information is not submitted within the 90-day timeframe, bills for all dates\nL62@P2: of service that exceed the authorized session limit will be returned and will\nL63@P2: not be considered for payment. However, bills for dates of service\nL64@P2: provided after the required information is received may be considered if\nL65@P2: the additional treatment is approved and the authorized session limit is\nL66@P2: increased.\nL67@P2: (d) Outpatient mental health services that exceed statutory maximums or for\nL68@P2: inpatient psychiatric, psychological, or other mental health counseling providers\nL69@P2: must submit the information outlined in §649.29.2 to the Board for approval\nL70@P2: before treatment may be considered for payment.\nL71@P2: (1) Providers must submit the information to the Board for review and\nL72@P2: approval within 90 days of the date the Board receives the bill for\nL73@P2: outpatient mental health services that exceed statutory maximums or for\nL74@P2: inpatient mental health treatment. If the required information is not\nL75@P2: submitted within the 90-day timeframe, bills for all dates of service that\nL76@P2: exceed statutory maximums or for inpatient mental health treatment will\nL77@P2: be returned and will not be considered for payment. However, bills for\nL78@P2: dates of service provided after the required information is received may\nL79@P2: be considered if the dire or exceptional treatment is approved.\nL80@P2: Note: Authority cited: Sections 13920 and 13974, Government Code.\nL81@P2-3: Reference: Sections 13957, 13957.2, and 13957.7 Government Code. 3\nL82@P3: § 649.29.1. Mental Health Benefits\nL83@P3: (a) The Board may reimburse a claimant for the expense of outpatient mental health\nL84@P3: services incurred as the direct result of a qualifying crime in an amount not to exceed\nL85@P3: the statutory benefit limits set forth in Government Code §13957(a)(2)(A) and (B) and\nL86@P3: consistent with Government Code §13959(d). Outpatient mental health services that\nL87@P3: may be reimbursed include, but are not limited to, the following:\nL88@P3: (1) In person or telehealth individual or family mental health\nL89@P3: therapy sessions;\nL90@P3: (2) Group therapy;\nL91@P3: (3) A maximum of five (5) hours of case management per claimant, which will\nL92@P3: not be counted as part of their mental health session limit;\nL93@P3: (4) Medication management;\nL94@P3: (5) Biofeedback therapy, when provided by a mental health provider\nL95@P3: authorized by the Board of Behavioral Sciences;\nL96@P3: (6) Hypnotherapy, when provided by a mental health provider authorized by\nL97@P3: the Board of Behavioral Sciences;\nL98@P3: (7) Music therapy, when provided by a mental health provider authorized by the\nL99@P3: Board of Behavioral Sciences;\nL100@P3: (8) Psychological and Neuropsychological testing;\nL101@P3: (9) Interpreter services received during mental health treatment; and\nL102@P3: (10) Transportation expenses to and from mental health appointments.\nL103@P3: (b) Claimants and/or providers must submit the information listed below to the Board\nL104@P3: with their initial request for reimbursement of mental health services. Sessions may be\nL105@P3: reimbursed once the required information has been provided to and approved by the\nL106@P3: Board. The required information includes:\nL107@P3: (1) The claimant’s name and CalVCB application number;\nL108@P3: (2) A brief description of the qualifying crime, including the date it occurred and\nL109@P3: any relevant details such as the suspect’s name and relationship to the victim;\nL110@P3: (3) The date treatment began and the date treatment terminated, if\nL111@P3: applicable;\nL112@P3: (4) A statement that the treatment is or is not necessary as a direct result of the\nL113@P3: qualifying crime;\nL114@P3: (5) The treating provider’s or therapist’s name, license number, contact\nL115@P3-4: information, and provider agency or organization name;4\nL116@P4: (6) The supervising provider’s name, license number, contact information, and\nL117@P4: provider agency or organization name, if applicable;\nL118@P4: (7) If an EOB or denial is unable to be provided, a statement indicating the\nL119@P4: reason why including, but not limited to: the network provider is located more\nL120@P4: than 45 miles from the claimant’s residence; the network provider is not able to\nL121@P4: provide treatment within 45 days of request due to scheduling issues; or the\nL122@P4: network provider has a limited number of Medi-Cal slots and all Medi-Cal slots\nL123@P4: have been filled;\nL124@P4: (8) A declaration of certification regarding the information in subsections (1)\nL125@P4: through (7) above, signed under penalty of perjury by the treating provider or\nL126@P4: therapist;\nL127@P4: (9) A declaration of certification regarding the information in subsections (1)\nL128@P4: through (7) above, signed under penalty of perjury by the supervising provider or\nL129@P4: therapist, if applicable;\nL130@P4: (10) A declaration of certification regarding the information in subsections (1)\nL131@P4: through (7) above, signed under penalty of perjury by the claimant.\nL132@P4: (c) Providers must complete a treatment plan at the beginning of treatment that\nL133@P4: includes the information listed below to document the treatment is necessary as a\nL134@P4: direct result of a qualifying crime. Treatment plans must include:\nL135@P4: (1) The claimant’s name and CalVCB application number;\nL136@P4: (2) A brief description of the qualifying crime, including the date it occurred and\nL137@P4: any relevant details such as the suspect’s name and relationship to the victim;\nL138@P4: (3) A statement estimating the percentage of treatment needed as a direct\nL139@P4: result of the qualifying crime;\nL140@P4: (4) If there was a delay in treatment of three years or longer, a description of the\nL141@P4: events, behaviors, or reasons the claimant waited to seek treatment;\nL142@P4: (5) If there was a break in treatment over one year, a description of the events,\nL143@P4: behaviors, or reasons the claimant paused treatment;\nL144@P4: (6) If the claimant was below age four when treatment began, explain what\nL145@P4: behaviors or symptomologies are being treated and how they are a result of the\nL146@P4: qualifying crime;\nL147@P4: (7) For post-crime primary caretakers, a statement as to whether the treatment is\nL148@P4: necessary for treatment of the minor direct victim;\nL149@P4: (8) The date treatment began, the most recent date of treatment, the date that\nL150@P4: treatment completed (if applicable), and the number of session hours provided\nL151@P4-5: and types of sessions provided;5\nL152@P5: (9) The treating therapist’s name, license number, contact information, and\nL153@P5: provider agency or organization name, if applicable;\nL154@P5: (10) The supervising therapist’s name, license number, contact information, and\nL155@P5: provider agency or organization name, if applicable;\nL156@P5: (11) A declaration of certification regarding the information in subsections (1)\nL157@P5: through (10) above, signed under penalty of perjury by the treating provider or\nL158@P5: therapist; and\nL159@P5: (12) A declaration of certification regarding the information in subsections (1)\nL160@P5: through (10) above, signed under penalty of perjury by the supervising provider\nL161@P5: or therapist, if applicable.\nL162@P5: (d) Treatment plans must be kept in the claimant’s file, except for the following\nL163@P5: circumstances when it must be submitted to the Board with the first request for\nL164@P5: reimbursement:\nL165@P5: (1) Upon the Board’s request; or\nL166@P5: (2) If treatment is less than 100 percent a direct result of the qualifying crime; or\nL167@P5: (3) There was a delay in treatment of three years; or\nL168@P5: (4) There was a break in treatment over one year; or\nL169@P5: (5) If the claimant was below age four when treatment began; or\nL170@P5: (6) If the treatment is for a post-crime primary caretaker.\nL171@P5: (e) Requests for additional mental health treatment sessions beyond the approved\nL172@P5: session limit must be submitted to the Board when the claimant is eight (8) sessions\nL173@P5: away from reaching their authorized session limit. The request must include the\nL174@P5: information listed below and be approved by the Board before additional sessions\nL175@P5: may be considered for payment. Requests for additional treatment must include:\nL176@P5: (1) The claimant’s name and CalVCB application number;\nL177@P5: (2) A brief description of the crime for which mental health sessions are being\nL178@P5: provided, including the date the crime occurred and any relevant details\nL179@P5: provided by the claimant;\nL180@P5: (3) The date treatment began, the most recent date of treatment, and the date\nL181@P5: treatment terminated, if applicable;\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegulations - CA Victim Compensation Board (https://victims.ca.gov/board/proposed-regulations/)\nciteturn1216view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1188view1\",\"id\":30}); Total lines: 46\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn1216view4 [wordlim: 200] Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1188view1\",\"id\":22}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn1216view5 [wordlim: 200] Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1185view0\",\"id\":46}); Total lines: 1\n"
